      <rules>
        <rule id="126d-98a9-b09b-c9b8" name="Sire of the Death Guard" publicationId="ca571888--pubN113187" page="47" hidden="false">
          <description>All models with the Legiones Astartes (Death Guard) rule in an army with Mortarion gain Stubborn (unless already Fearless).  Frag grenades, frag missiles, and Havoc Launchers in the army gain Poisoned (4)</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="4b14-d5b2-6e93-ffbc" name="Shadow of the Reaper" publicationId="ca571888--pubN113187" page="47" hidden="false">
          <description>Leadership tests taken from Fear caused by Mortarion are taken at a -1 penalty. In addition, in lieu of making a run or shooting attack, as long as he is not locked in combat or inside a transport, he may attempt to redeploy by passing a leadership test.  If passed, Mortarion may be re-deployed anywhere within 10" of his starting position as long as he is 3" away from any enemy model. If part of a unit, he automatically separates.  May charge on the turn this is used, but counts as a Disordered Charge.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="4f33-f522-ee24-7eba" name="Preturnatural Resiliance" publicationId="ca571888--pubN113187" page="47" hidden="false">
          <description>- Re-rolls any failed Toughness tests or It Will Not Die rolls
- Automatically passes Dangerous Terrain tests
- Any weapon which wounds without regard to Mortarion's toughness (ie Poison or otherwise) only affect Mortarion on a 6 instead of their usual effect.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="a617-a889-0f31-9b9d" name="Witch-Spite" page="" hidden="false">
          <description>Any Malediction power affecting Mortarion or a unit he has joined is negated on a 4.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
