          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Unit Type" typeId="556e6974205479706523232344415441232323">Infantry (Character)</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="WS" typeId="575323232344415441232323">6</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="BS" typeId="425323232344415441232323">5</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="S" typeId="5323232344415441232323">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="T" typeId="5423232344415441232323">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="W" typeId="5723232344415441232323">3</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="I" typeId="4923232344415441232323">5</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="A" typeId="4123232344415441232323">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="LD" typeId="4c4423232344415441232323">10</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Save" typeId="5361766523232344415441232323">3+</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule id="0fc6-3c9b-6db6-11dd" name="The Bloody Aegis" publicationId="690c-3e82-3080-6bc0" page="189" hidden="false">
          <description>Increases Ophion's invulnerable save to 3+ in close combat.  In addition, any model that targets Ophion with one or more attacks in an assault and scores an unmodified 1 on at least one of those dice, has its WS halved when targeted by any of Ophion's close combat attacks until the beginning of the next Game Turn.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="855c-ba1a-2c1a-c2ff" name="The Coward" publicationId="690c-3e82-3080-6bc0" page="189" hidden="false">
          <description>Once Ophion has lost a single wound, he gains Feel No Pain (4+).  When reduced to a single wound remaining, upgraded to Feel No Pain (3+).</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="c50d-3c0d-01ab-5454" name="Warlord: Aberrant Bravery" publicationId="690c-3e82-3080-6bc0" page="189" hidden="false">
          <description>If Kheron Ophion is the army's warlord then as long as Ophion's controlling player has less Victory points than their opponent, Ophion and any Night Lords units within 12'' of him gain the Stubborn special rule. Additionally, the controlling player may always choose to re-roll, or have his opponent re-roll, any failed dice roll to determine if the game continues for another turn.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
