      <rules>
        <rule id="5751-0d6c-40db-a322" name="Warlord: Inspiring Presence" hidden="false">
          <description>Friendly units within 12" of the Warlord can use the Warlord's Leadership rather than their own.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="309c-da21-55e9-e5d7" name="Ally of the Silent Order" publicationId="ca571888--pubN92115" page="225" hidden="false">
          <description>A single Sister of Silence Oblivion Knight-Centura may be selected as part of Tsolmon Khan's unit as long as he is not mounted on a Scimitar Jetbike, at the start of the game during deployment - these two models must remain part of the same unit. After having been deployed onto the battlefield, they may in subsquent turns operate as separate Independent Characters.
In addition, Tsolmon Khan does not reduce his Leadership value due to the proximity to models with the Psychic Anathema special rule, and if he uses the Glorious Intervention special rule to intercede in a Challange involving a friendly Sisters of Silence character, then he gains an additional attack from the duration of that Challenge. If this is used in the same turn as The Hammerhand special rules, then the +1 Attack bonus may be used to increase the number of Attacks made from 1 to 2.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="ed9e-c491-0871-da3b" name="The Hammerhand" publicationId="ca571888--pubN92115" page="225" hidden="false">
          <description>On any turn in which Tsolmon Khan has succussfully charged an enemy unit, the controlling player may choose to, instead of making his normal allotment of close combat attacks, instead make a single attack using Tsolmon Khan's master-crafted thunder hammer at this normal Initiative, ignoring the Unwieldy special rule.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <infoLinks>
